account credentials (console login, or an UPSTASH_EMAIL + management
API key pair) were available in this execution context -- verified:
no UPSTASH_EMAIL/UPSTASH_API_KEY in the shell env, no UPSTASH_* secret
in Secret Manager beyond the existing (unpaired) UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN,
no persisted browser session at console.upstash.com (confirmed: fresh
navigation landed on the login form, not a signed-in dashboard).
Provisioning a NEW Upstash database requires interactive account access
this agent does not have. Escalating to the operator; see close note in
_scratch/76j-workstream-c.md.

What follows is a REAL burst test run against the deployed service in
its CURRENT state (UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL is a Secret-Manager-bound
placeholder value; PR #57 fail-loud degraded-mode code is live). It
documents the honest current behavior and one adjacent finding; it does
NOT and cannot demonstrate a shared cross-instance budget, because there
is no shared store to demonstrate.

